\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{Begin from the precise set-level augmented-VDC operations and equations. The generating graph signature has objects, vertical and horizontal edges, and cells with ordered input paths and either one or zero horizontal outputs, including \code{(0,0)} cells. Write all incidence maps, both vertical-cell compositions, identities, and substitution equations before constructing the free monad. Prove monadicity/arity hypotheses if the BMW route is used.}
  \p{Unaugmented substitution has a useful row description with shared vertical sides; where proved, a row corresponds to an active map \code{[k] → [n]}. This does not extend to all augmented shapes as an ordinary active chain: an input path of length one and empty output has no associated active \code{[0] → [1]}. Candidate augmented data therefore records the full input/output paths, cells including empty-output cells, vertical boundaries, and their incidence/substitution structure. Rows with output flags are a proposed serialization only. Their valid composites, normalization, morphisms, and arity theorem must be proved before they become the canonical format. A specialized algebraic presentation remains acceptable if rows fail.}
  \p{The early examples include \code{c₁^∅}, \code{(0,0)} cells and both compositions, nullary inputs, shared-side compositions, and mixed rows. The no-horizontal fragment must recover 2-categories by the discrete nerve comparison.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Augmentation changes the combinatorics; serialization cannot establish it.}
  \p{The current presentation separates incident row shapes from cell labels and centralizes transport along equality of complete boundaries. The algebra equations use ordinary equality after that transport. Rationale for this provisional refinement: substitution incidence must be independent of labels, and clients should not repeatedly reconstruct dependent reindexing. Checked round trips preserve the existing rows; this does not establish canonical arities.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{The previous assertion that all augmented arities are chains of active maps in ordinary Δ; inferring a general pasting theorem from a row picture.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{\ref{at-fd-0007}, \ref{at-kr-0008}; \ref{at-kr-0003} only after the explicit presentation exists.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{provisional algebra presentation; arity and diagram-model results remain open.}
  \p{\ref{augmented-algebra} records the equation families, their dependent incidence proofs and a nontrivial lawful additive-label model. \ref{augmented-transport} records the revised API, renewed model evidence, strict 2-category extraction, and reverse operation data. \ref{augmented-comparison} adds the reverse algebra, cell/hom round trips, arbitrary substitution compatibility and discrete hom nerves. The actual arity presentation, augmented nerve recognition hypotheses and labelled diagram model remain open under \ref{at-fd-0007}. Rationale for retaining provisional status: this checked slice does not supply the full comparison, arity or homotopical model the root requires.}
}

\p{\strong{Relative free-cell evidence:} \ref{augmented-free-cells} proves the generated-congruence quotient laws and universal mapping property over a fixed vertical category and horizontal graph, with finite raw-term support. \ref{augmented-generating} extends this to an explicit generating presheaf base, free vertical paths and a global free mapping property. \ref{augmented-global-adjunction} adds the checked global free/forgetful adjunction and induced monad. Monadicity is now proved in \ref{augmented-monadicity}; the arity density and exactness hypotheses remain open.}

\p{\strong{Monad-algebra reconstruction evidence:} \ref{augmented-monad-vertical} reconstructs vertical categories and functors from arbitrary generating-monad algebras, retains the horizontal graph and proves a natural equivalence recovering each existing augmented algebra's vertical category. \ref{augmented-monad-cells} adds incident cells, all primitive operations and a surjective full-boundary evaluation map preserving both identities and arbitrary substitution. \ref{augmented-monadicity} now proves all five reconstructed equation families, identifies the action and proves essential surjectivity and monadicity. \ref{augmented-arity-nerve} constructs the actual nerve square and its canonical comparison, proving conditional recognition under density and comparison invertibility. Choosing and proving the diagram arities and the labelled diagram model remain open.}
